/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  flashComplex -- the case the architecture had to grow to serve.  It was
  written as a DESIGN DRIVER: a case the engine could not run, whose every
  refusal named a slice of work.  Every one of those slices has landed, and
  the case now runs.  What it drove:

      the SECOND LIQUID on the reactive path   (chemistry and two liquids
                                                at once -- the fork closed)
      GENERAL SALT RECONSTRUCTION              (m = A n, and the rank test
                                                that refuses an ambiguous basis)
      the HENRY rung for a permanent gas       (N2 is not a backbone co-solvent)
      the STREAM BASIS                         (components and species, both
                                                visible on every stream)

  FOUR PHASES in one vessel, at 308.15 K and 2 atm:

      vapour          N2 (inert, guarantees V > 0) + CO2 + NH3 + H2S + H2O +
                      ethanol + benzene
      aqueous liquid  water solvent, carbonate + ammonia + sulfide + acetate
                      networks, Ca+2, dissolved N2
      organic liquid  benzene solvent; by DECLARED admission only ethanol may
                      join it (water/ion exclusion = announced approximation)
      solid           calcite CaCO3 -- fed, and it GROWS: the free water sits
                      at SI +0.788, so 1.52e-3 mol/kg precipitates to the
                      SI = 0 ceiling

  A FIFTH phase is designed for and NOT admitted: NH4HCO3, which is never fed
  and would appear if the NH3 + CO2 loading crossed saturation.  Its
  equilibrium is not curated and the case refuses to invent one -- see
  constant/NH4HCO3.dat and constant/chemistryDict.  That is the demonstration
  still owed: a solid the student never wrote entering the answer.

  THE ANSWER.  V/F = 0.0635; the bottoms at pH 8.341 against a feed whose own
  liquid sits at 6.917 (the CO2 leaving for the vapour is the difference);
  the organic liquid 23.3 % of the backbone liquid at 95 % benzene; |r|max
  7e-14 in 6 outer iterations with a quadratic tail.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

application   choupoSolve;
description  "FlashComplex: 4-phase reactive flash -- vapour + two liquids (declared admission) + growing calcite, N2 inert on the Henry rung.  It DEMONSTRATES that the joint Newton closes (|r| 2e-13, V/F 0.0635, organic 23.3 % of the liquid); it does NOT predict the chemistry -- the ions are Davies on water-referenced molality in a backbone that is ~10 mol% ethanol, and the mixed-solvent transfer term that would price that is a NAMED GAP, worth ~2 log units on the calcite SI.  The pH is an OUTPUT of that model, not a claim about this water";
verbosity     3;

reports
{
    streamTable    { }
    massBalance    { }
    elementBalance { }
}
